  "description": "Are a DAO owner and an ACE OLE DB (ADO) owner in one process both admitted for different rows of one page, and does the ADO commit survive the DAO Rollback? DAO owner A = Workspaces(0) with OpenDatabase(A, writable). ADO owner = ADODB.Connection with Provider = Microsoft.ACE.OLEDB.12.0 and Properties('Data Source') = A, Open. A: BeginTrans; UPDATE T SET V = 9 WHERE ID = 1 (dbFailOnError). ADO: BeginTrans (its return value is the nesting level); Execute UPDATE T SET V = 101 WHERE ID = 5 (adCmdText | adExecuteNoRecords); Connection.Errors. ADO CommitTrans; DAO Rollback; DBEngine.Errors and Connection.Errors; read T through DAO; close; read T through a fresh Workspace.",
